184}\n   * CVE-2026-89861\n     - scsi: qla2xxx: Hold vport reference in qla24xx_report_id_acquisition()\n       {CVE-2026-89861}\n   * CVE-2026-53078\n     - bpf: Fix same-register dst/src OOB read and pointer leak in sock_ops\n       {CVE-2026-53078}\n   * CVE-2026-64565\n     - Input: ims-pcu - fix heap-buffer-overflow in ims_pcu_process_data()\n       {CVE-2026-64565}\n   * CVE-2026-89631\n     - smb: client: reject a tree connect response whose byte count is too small\n       {CVE-2026-89631}\n   * CVE-2026-46075\n     - crypto: atmel-sha204a - Fix potential UAF and memory leak in remove path\n       {CVE-2026-46075}\n   * CVE-2026-74724\n     - ipvs: avoid out-of-bounds write in ip_vs_nat_icmp {CVE-2026-74724}\n   * CVE-2026-63956\n     - USB: serial: cypress_m8: fix memory corruption with small endpoint\n       {CVE-2026-63956}\n   * Miscellaneous upstream changes\n     - nfsd: hold cl_lock in client_has_openowners()\n     - sctp: hold transport reference across connect wait\n     - fbcon: Avoid using FNTCHARCNT() and hard-coded built-in font charcount\n     - ALSA: caiaq: Fix potential double-free at error path\n     - KVM: SVM: Fix offset computation bug in __sev_dbg_decrypt().\n     - mm: split critical region in remap_file_pages() and invoke LSMs in between\n     - drivers: base: cacheinfo: Fix shared_cpu_map changes in event of CPU\n       hotplug\n     - scsi: qla2xxx: Hold vport_slock for host map update in report ID\n       acquisition\n     - cifs: validate full SID length in security descriptors\n     - ocfs2/heartbeat: fix slot mapping rollback leaks on error paths\n     - firewire: core: validate parent port count before allocating nodes in\n       build_tree()\n     - Input: ims-pcu - fix logic error in packet reset\n     - scsi: qla2xxx: Drop vport reference under lock in report ID acquisition\n     - bpf: sock_ops ctx access may stomp registers in corner case\n     - cpufreq: Abort show()/store() for half-initialized policies\n     - media: rtl